-- title:
--   Completed node ring as crossing model W[[U,V]]/(UV-π^E)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a natural number $N\neq 0$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring homomorphism $red\colon A\to k$, modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality of the two Hecke maps at level $N$ and $q$, and a place specialisation $P$ for these data; let $R$ be a prolongation tuple over $P$, with $k$ algebraically closed and $q\nmid N$. Assume $R$ is a model (the two divisor laws and the two cusp laws), that $W_0$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` each of which is supersingular (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set), that $R$ satisfies the regularity law and the node-value law on $W_0$ and the order law at the $\varphi^2$-fixed affine places, and fix a number field $K\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $w\in W_0$. Suppose the ring $R_w =$ `R.nodeIntegersOver K w` (functions integral for both prolongations, integral at every place of the level-$Nq$ curve reducing to $w$, and lying in the field generated over $K$) is local and Noetherian, and that $\varpi\in A\cap K$ generates the kernel of the reduction restricted to $A\cap K$, in the sense that $d$ reduces to $0$ exactly when $\varpi\mid d$. Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, $\pi$ an irreducible element, and $\sigma\colon W\to\widehat{R_w}$ a ring homomorphism into the adic completion of $R_w$ at its maximal ideal sending $\pi$ to the constant function attached to $\varpi$ and such that every element of $R_w$ agrees with some $\sigma(o)$ modulo the ideal generated by the maximal ideal. Then there is an exponent $E\geq 1$, a node-coordinate datum $c=(x,y)$ at $w$ over $K$ (so the first residue of $x$ vanishes and its second residue has order $1$ at the Frobenius translate of $w$, while the second residue of $y$ vanishes and its first residue has order $1$ at $w$) and a unit $u$ of $R_w$ with $xy = \varpi^{E}u$, together with a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from $\widehat{R_w}$ onto `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ E)`, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring over $W$ by $(UV-\pi^{E})$, and units $\alpha,\beta$ there, such that $\iota(\sigma(o))$ is the constant $o$ for every $o\in W$, $\iota(x)=U\alpha$ and $\iota(y)=V\beta$, and the branch orders are read off: for $f\in R_w$ and $n\in\mathbb{N}$, if the first residue of $f$ is nonzero with order $n$ at $w$ then $\iota(f)\equiv\gamma V^{n}$ modulo the ideal generated by $\pi$ and $U$ for some unit $\gamma$, and symmetrically, if the second residue of $f$ is nonzero with order $n$ at the Frobenius translate of $w$ then $\iota(f)\equiv\gamma U^{n}$ modulo the ideal generated by $\pi$ and $V$ for some unit $\gamma$.
--
--   This is the local structure of the model of $X_0(Nq)$ at a supersingular point in the formalisation's axiomatic setting: the completed local ring is a crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^{E})$, presented so that the two node coordinates are unit multiples of $U$ and $V$ and so that the isomorphism computes the orders of the two branch residues. It is used downstream to produce annuli and component charts at such a point, and to pin down uniquely the place reducing to $w$ on which a node coordinate takes a prescribed value.
